From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] MIPS: dts: ingenic: t41: bring up the SFC and SPI NOR

The stock T41 tree names the flash controller "ingenic,sfc", which no
mainline driver matches, and gives it no clock and no flash child. The
7.3.1 spi-ingenic-sfc driver matches "ingenic,t41-sfc"/"ingenic,x2000-sfc",
requires the "sfc" clock, and only creates an MTD device for a child
SPI NOR node.

Attach it to the CGU, describe the flash as jedec,spi-nor, and drop the
vendor pinctrl state, which the mainline pinctrl driver cannot map;
U-Boot has already muxed the SFC pins. The resulting controller gets
bus number 0, so the U-Boot mtdparts=spi0.0 argument partitions it and
mtdblock4 becomes the rootfs.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
--- a/arch/mips/boot/dts/ingenic/t41.dtsi
+++ b/arch/mips/boot/dts/ingenic/t41.dtsi
@@ -429,13 +429,21 @@
 		};
 
 		sfc0: sfc0@0x13440000 {
-			compatible = "ingenic,sfc";
+			compatible = "ingenic,t41-sfc", "ingenic,x2000-sfc";
 			reg = <0x13440000 0x10000>;
+			clocks = <&clock T41_CLK_SFC0>;
+			clock-names = "sfc";
+			#address-cells = <1>;
+			#size-cells = <0>;
 			interrupt-parent = <&core_intc>;
 			interrupts = <IRQ_SFC0>;
-			pinctrl-names = "default";
-			pinctrl-0 = <&sfc0_pa>;
 			status = "okay";
+
+			flash@0 {
+				compatible = "jedec,spi-nor";
+				reg = <0>;
+				spi-max-frequency = <25000000>;
+			};
 		};
 
 		sfc1: sfc1@0x13450000 {
